SUMMARY:POM Workshop at Marietta Cellar's Tasting Room
DESCRIPTION:There's something deeply satisfying about making something fluffy\, colorful\, and entirely your own — and Marietta Cellars' downtown Healdsburg tasting room is the most delightful place to do it. On Sunday\, April 26\, join creative instructor Naomi for a POM Workshop: an irresistibly fun introduction to the timeless art of pom pom making\, surrounded by the warmth of one of Sonoma County's most beloved wineries.Using a vibrant array of yarns in every imaginable color\, guests will learn to craft pom poms of any size — perfect for adorning a keychain\, brightening up a rearview mirror\, or decking out a holiday tree (and beyond). All materials are provided and no prior experience is necessary\, making this a wonderful outing for families\, friends\, and crafters of every skill level. Expect laughter\, colorful chaos\, and the joy of taking home something handmade you'll actually love.Priced at $103\, the workshop includes light snacks and a first pour of Marietta wine. It's the perfect Sunday morning spent with great wine\, great company\, and your hands joyfully submerged in a sea of beautiful yarn.
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/pom-workshop-at-marietta-cellars-tasting-room/
LOCATION:CA
CATEGORIES:Arts,Crafts,Experiences
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://winecountry-media.s3.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/5/2026/04/08042228/pom-workshop-3.jpg
END:VEVENT
